{"id":"813a9fa8-e01e-468a-93ae-210f830827e6","article_key":"doi:10.1016/j.cell.2026.09.008","title":"Single-cell analysis of chromatin state and transcriptome in the human basal ganglia","title_zh":"人类基底神经节染色质状态和转录组单细胞分析","doi":"10.1016/j.cell.2026.09.008","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.cell.2026.09.008","abstract":"The basal ganglia are central to motor control, learning, emotion, and reward processing, and their dysfunction contributes to many neurological and psychiatric disorders. Here, we generated a single-cell multi-omic atlas of histone modifications and transcriptomes across eight basal ganglia regions from neurotypical human donors. This atlas resolved cell-type- and region-specific landscapes of active and repressive candidate cis-regulatory elements and delineated gene regulatory networks underlying cell identity. We found that the combinatorial expression of homeobox transcription factors provides distinctive molecular descriptors of neuronal cell identities in the basal ganglia. Integration with matched MERFISH spatial transcriptomics further uncovered regional heterogeneity in epigenomic and transcriptional programs. Finally, we used this atlas to interpret noncoding risk variants associated with neuropsychiatric disorders and to construct a deep-learning model that predicts gene regulatory activities and variant effects. Together, this work provides a multimodal regulatory framework for understanding human basal ganglia organization, evolution, and disease genetics.","abstract_zh":"基底神经节对于运动控制、学习、情绪和奖赏处理至关重要，其功能障碍与许多神经和精神疾病相关。在此研究中，我们构建了来自神经正常人类供体八个基底神经节区域的组蛋白修饰和转录组单细胞多组学图谱。该图谱揭示了活跃与抑制性候调控元件在细胞类型和区域特异性方面的景观，并勾勒了细胞身份的基因调控网络。我们发现，同源框转录因子的组合表达为基底神经节神经元细胞身份提供了独特的分子标记。与匹配的MERFISH空间转录组整合进一步揭示了表观基因组和转录组程序的区域异质性。最后，我们利用该图谱解释与神经精神疾病相关的非编码风险变异，并构建了一种深度学习模型来预测基因调控活性和变异效应。共同，这项工作为理解人类基底神经节的组织、进化和疾病遗传学提供了多模态调控框架。","snippet":"The basal ganglia are central to motor control, learning, emotion, and reward processing, and their dysfunction contributes to many neurological and psychiatric disorders. Here, we generated a single-cell multi-omic atlas of histone modifications and transcriptomes across eight basal ganglia regions from neurotypical human donors. This atlas resolved cell-type- and region-specific landscapes of active and repressive…","translated_at":"2026-11-14T08:11:26.352478Z","translation_model":"nvidia/nemotron-3.5-super-vl-120b-a12b","source_category":"doi","article_type":"journal-article","volume":"189","issue":"23","published_at":"2026-11-01T00:00:00","acquired_at":"2026-11-12T23:34:37Z","display_date":"2026-11-12T23:34:37Z","display_date_source":"acquired","online_published_at":null,"print_published_at":"2026-11-01T00:00:00","first_author":"Lei Chang","authors_text":"Lei Chang, Kai Li, Yang Xie, Guojie Zhong, Jonathan A. Rink, Cindy Tatiana Báez-Becerra, Audrey Lie, Hannah S. Indralingam, Timothy Loe, Keyi Dong, Xiaomeng Gao, Zhaoning Wang, Songpeng Zu, Joseph Colin Kern, Zoey Zhao, Eric Boone, Jesus Flores, Alexander Monell, Jacqueline Olness, Cesar Barragan, Emma Osgood, William Owens, Natalie Schenker-Ahmed, Wenjin Zhang, Di Liu, Ariana S. Barcoma, Jackson K. Willier, Kyle W. Knutson, Kaitlyn G. Russo, Jiayi Liu, Silvia Cho, Jessica Arzavala, Carissa K. Young, Guha V. Sundaram, Austin C. Manning, Yareli Sanchez, Aleksandra Bikkina, Jillian V. Berry, Carolyn O’Connor, Michelle Liem, Mikayla V. Marrin, Cynthia Rose, Shane N. Alt, Chenxu Zhu, Nathan R. Zemke, Wubin Ding, Amit Klein, Yuanyuan Fu, Nelson Johansen, Trygve E. Bakken, Rebecca D. Hodge, C. Dirk Keene, Ed S. Lein, Daofeng Li, Quan Zhu, Ting Wang, Xiangmin Xu, Joseph R. Ecker, M. Margarita Behrens, Bing Ren","authors":[{"position":0,"given_name":"Lei","family_name":"Chang","full_name":"Lei Chang","affiliation":null},{"position":1,"given_name":"Kai","family_name":"Li","full_name":"Kai Li","affiliation":null},{"position":2,"given_name":"Yang","family_name":"Xie","full_name":"Yang Xie","affiliation":null},{"position":3,"given_name":"Guojie","family_name